ndice de exposicion table say). The current English copy (H-1-5213, revised 3-26, kodak-vision3-200t.pdf) has the same plots as raster images with the same curves and axis labels; the vector copy was used for its exact curve paths. Labels in the Spanish copy: Curvas sensitometricas, Curvas de sensibilidad espectral, Curvas de la densidad espectral de los colorantes.","Exposure indexes printed: tungsten (3000 K and 3200 K) 200, daylight (5500 K) 125 with the Wratten 2 / 85 filter; the curves are for 3200 K, 1/50 s, so balance is tungsten and iso 200.","Characteristic curves: the top axis (log exposure, lux-seconds) is printed with only three labels: -3.684 at the left frame, -1.284 in the middle and 1.116 at the right frame; the bottom axis gives camera stops -8 to +8 over the same width (stop 0 = log -1.284). The x axis is the printed log exposure as read from those labels, a 4.8 log unit range (16 stops); the 500T sheet uses a 5.0 range. Densitometry: Status M.","No Log H Ref or grey-card density table is printed, so log_h_ref is null.","Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/25 s, ECN-2, Status M, density 0.2 above D-min; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in erg/cm2) as printed. The yellow-forming layer (b) is drawn from about 380 to 520 nm, magenta (g) 480 to 600 nm, cyan (r) 560 to 680 nm; the lines stop where Kodak stops them.","Spectral dye density: ECN-2, D-mins subtracted, diffuse density; the cyan, magenta and yellow curves are peak-normalised (peak 1.0), mid is the Midscale Neutral curve (Escala media neutra) and min the dashed Minimum Density curve (Densidad minima).","Grain: the sheet gives diffuse rms granularity curves only (48 micrometre aperture, ECN-2; Sigma D scale on the right, multiply by 1000), no single printed value, so grain is null. Read by eye, Sigma D is roughly 0.005 to 0.009 for the green and red records (rms about 5 to 9) and 0.011 to 0.016 for the blue record, depending on density.","Print film: none is named on the sheet; LAD values are said to be specific to each print or duplicating film."],"print":"kodak-2383"}